        intro: "Let's learn the deep Classical Pirc plan! After **6.O-O O-O** the basic Classical Pirc lesson ends — but real games keep going. The standard Black plan from move 6 onward is **…c6** preparing **…b5**, then if White plays the prophylactic **a4** stopping the pawn push, we switch to **…a5** + **…Na6-c7** + **…Bg4** + **…e5** — a slow positional manoeuvring middlegame. This is the Pirc tabiya competitive Black players reach almost every game, where understanding the IDEAS (knight reroutes, central breaks, when to trade dark-square bishops) outweighs memorisation. If you only learn one Pirc tabiya, learn this one.",
